WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.272
In the Warring States period, Shang Yang came to Qin and sought an audience with Duke Xiao.

00:00:04.622 --> 00:00:07.310
He brought with him a way to make the state strong.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.972
Duke Xiao was searching for talent that could make Qin strong.

00:00:11.322 --> 00:00:14.994
To make the people trust the new laws, Shang Yang set up a pole to establish credibility.

00:00:15.344 --> 00:00:18.656
The man who carried the pole away truly received the reward money.

00:00:19.006 --> 00:00:21.958
From then on, everyone knew the state's word counted.

00:00:22.308 --> 00:00:25.236
Shang Yang valued agriculture and redistributed the land.

00:00:25.586 --> 00:00:28.418
Farmers who worked hard at their fields could earn rewards.

00:00:28.768 --> 00:00:31.048
The fields multiplied, and the granaries slowly filled.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:33.966
He also used military merit to decide soldiers' rank.

00:00:34.316 --> 00:00:37.076
Those who earned merit could raise their own status.

00:00:37.426 --> 00:00:40.858
The people found that hard work truly could change their lives.

00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:44.616
The old nobles disliked the new laws and often opposed Shang Yang.

00:00:44.966 --> 00:00:47.966
But Duke Xiao supported him, and the reforms continued.

00:00:48.316 --> 00:00:51.676
Shang Yang said: before the law, everyone must obey.

00:00:52.026 --> 00:00:55.266
After Duke Xiao died, Shang Yang was put to death.

00:00:55.616 --> 00:00:58.928
But his new laws continued to shape the state of Qin.

00:00:59.278 --> 00:01:01.558
And so Qin moved, step by step, toward strength.

